Z||000000||Eric||05-13-99||07:17 PM||||I was thinking of doing an interior restoration on my car and was wondering if I could repaint the plastic dash.  It is faded in places and has black gashes where the gray paint has rubbed off.  What kind of paint should I use? <p>TIP: I notice alot of fieros have the console plastic coming apart from the frame.  I tried all sorts of glue (RVT, weatherstrip glue etc.)and the best thing is Krazy glue.  You can only get small portions but a little goes a long way and it dries so fast you don't even need a clamp for most applications.
Z||000001||theogre||05-13-99||07:47 PM||||yes you can paint it, but you have to make sure the paint is rated for that aplication. even then you want to try it on something scrap first. useing a couple light coats is best. otherwise you lose the surface texture.
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-14-99||10:08 AM||||Use paint made for Vinyl and plastic surfaces.  You can get it in spray cans.  I have a grey metallic 85SE with the light grey interior and found an exact match for the light grey.  I repainted all of the scuffed up trim and you can't tell what was repainted from the original.<br>I also repainted a 66 mustang dash many moons ago.  It lasted the 7 years that I kept the car.<br>Don't use regular spray paint (Krylon, etc) as it won't stick very long on the plastic.<br>Good luck,<br>Carroll
Z||000003||burdell1||05-15-99||12:00 AM||||Carroll,<p>What is the brand and paint # (if possible) for the paint you use for the interior (my 85 GT  also has a light grey interior)<p>Todd<br>
Z||000004||Eric||05-15-99||05:42 PM||||I just got done taking out my dash to repaint it.  When I first decided to take it out, I had no idea how long it would take.  I spent about 4 hours taking out everything that was in the dashboard's way, including the gauge cluster.  It was a tough job!  
Z||000005||rcn491||05-15-99||11:16 PM||||Eastwood sells a plastic paint for interiors<br>in 15 colors. I haven't tried it, so I don't<br>know if their gray would match.
